course: dictionary
lesson: 4662
title: Hockey: one word, different games
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word hockey can name more than one game, and which game it means depends on where you are. In the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand, it usually means field hockey, played on grass. In Canada and the USA, it usually means ice hockey.
explain: Context tells you which game is meant. «In ice hockey, where players chase a puck (a flat rubber disc), the stick is kept below the shoulders.» The words ice and puck are the clues. The brackets also explain what a puck is, which is a useful trick authors often use.
explain: Look at the place too. «In Montreal, Jules goes to grown-up dinners and chats easily about hockey and politics.» Montreal is in Canada, so hockey there probably means ice hockey. Use the clues in the text, then check: does your meaning still make sense in the sentence?
fact: Hockey is a team game played with curved sticks and a ball or puck, where players try to hit it into the other team's goal.
fact: Field hockey is played on grass with a ball.
fact: Ice hockey is played on ice with skates and a flat rubber disc called a puck.
fact: «A mouthguard protects the teeth in sports like hockey, rugby and basketball.»
fact: Players wear shin pads, gum shields and helmets, and keep their sticks low, to stay safe.
exercise: «Field hockey is played on grass with a ball.» Where is field hockey played? | On ice | *On grass | In a swimming pool | On a stage
exercise: «In ice hockey, where players chase a puck (a flat rubber disc).» What is a puck? | *A flat rubber disc | A helmet | A curved stick | A goal net
exercise: «In ice hockey, the stick is kept below the shoulders, because a high stick can injure faces.» Why must the stick be kept low? | *To stop a high stick injuring faces | To make the stick look smart | To make the ball go higher
test: In Canada, which game does the word hockey usually mean? | Rugby | *Ice hockey | Field hockey | Basketball
test: «A mouthguard protects the teeth in sports like hockey, rugby and basketball.» What does a mouthguard protect? | The knees | The eyes | The ankles | *The teeth
exam: «A cricket or hockey ball is hard enough to break bones, so close fielders and goalies wear helmets and pads.» Why do goalies wear helmets and pads? | *Because the ball is hard enough to break bones | Because helmets are fashionable | Because goalies are always cold | Because pads make them run faster
